     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Jun 29, 2020 at 11:53 AM Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks, Will. BTW the discrete logical in this code is in reference to whether mirt() or mdirt() was initially called as in indicates whether the latent variables are continuous (IRT) or discrete (e.g., latent class), not MG estimation. Cheers.<div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Jun 26, 2020 at 6:58 AM &#39;Will Belzak&#39; via mirt-package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Stain,<div><br></div><div>In the mirt package code (see line 125-127 at <a href=\"https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/blob/master/R/M2.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/blob/master/R/M2.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472275992000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1xnnkWXWA9jC3nmqwUTOAK\">https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/blob/master/R/M2.R</a>), a high-dimensional IRT model appears to correspond to any model that has more than 3 factors and is not a multiple-groups model (I think that&#39;s what &#39;discrete&#39; stands for in the code below).</div><div><br></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/attach/216a80eaa5d51/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"margin-right:0px\"><br></div><div><font color=\"#24292e\" face=\"-apple-system, system-ui, Segoe UI, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, Apple Color Emoji, Segoe UI Emoji\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Best,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#24292e\" face=\"-apple-system, system-ui, Segoe UI, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, Apple Color Emoji, Segoe UI Emoji\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Will</span></font></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Jun 26, 2020 at 4:49 AM stain stanley &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mailtoy...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">       M2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">df_irt_gpcm</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>           M2   df p     RMSEA   RMSEA_5  RMSEA_95     SRMSR        TLI CFI<br>stats </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1815656</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1531</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.3789824</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.3784966</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.3794224</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.4624416</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.3785642</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">   </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Warning</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> message</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">High</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dimensional models should </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">use</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> quasi</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Monte</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Carlo</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> integration</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Pass</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> QMC</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TRUE <br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">       M2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">df_irt_gpcm</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">QMC</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>            M2   df p     RMSEA   RMSEA_5  RMSEA_95     SRMSR       TLI      CFI<br>stats </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">213611.4</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1531</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.1295793</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.1291082</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.1300354</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.4354466</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.8388388</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.844819</span></div></code></div><br><br>I noticed significant difference between 2 results of above script.The only difference of script is `QMC=TRUE`.  <br>I want to know,how many dimensions should be regard as `High-dimensional`?<br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;mirt-package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-package...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/mirt-package/6e09ef25-1c48-4f57-96f7-8b1475873199o%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/mirt-package/6e09ef25-1c48-4f57-96f7-8b1475873199o%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472275992000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Tbp0MY64vbia6cmxzT87p\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/mirt-package/6e09ef25-1c48-4f57-96f7-8b1475873199o%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"font-family:Times\"><tbody><tr style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:sans-serif\"><td nowrap style=\"border-top:2px solid rgb(213,15,37)\">Will Belzak |</td><td nowrap style=\"border-top:2px solid rgb(51,105,232)\"> Data Science Intern |</td><td nowrap style=\"border-top:2px solid rgb(0,153,57)\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">wbe